    154  f080							; ==============================================================================
    155  f080							; TitleBand — merged title, bands 1-3 (N=4 layout, 2026-10-24).
    156  f080							; Band 0 is drawn by the CAVE kernel (stage PF + COLUPF from the room buffers,
    157  f080							; player via PlayerColTable/Grp0Ptr), so the title reuses the real kernel
    158  f080							; instead of duplicating its band rendering. The bank0 row-advance tail
    159  f080							; diverts here when DropTarget=$FF, exactly where band 1 would start.
    160  f080							; This routine: band 1 = stage row 1 (PREVIEW ONLY), band 2 = the TITLE PAD
    161  f080							; (playfield blanked, 48px S.A.V.I.O.R. logo + credit footer), band 3 = stage
    162  f080							; row 3, then the HUD band (score = level+1, lives/bombs/bar via MenuMain).
    163  f080							; Why the split (user ruling 2026-10-24): with 36-line bands the text no longer
    164  f080							; fitted under the player inside band 1 — the miner (band 0, Y 24..35) ran
    165  f080							; straight into the logo. Preview up top, text one band lower, keeps the two
    166  f080							; cleanly apart. No object is drawn on the title: DropArm .DATitle clears
    167  f080							; EnemyCount/LevelMinerRoom and the laser on every title LoadLevel, so
    168  f080							; SelectActiveObject parks GRP1.
    169  f080							; Entered via CallPad_TitleBand ($FC55). ZP: LineCount ($84) + Temp ($88) as
    170  f080							; loop counter/tmp — idle on title frames (cave overscan bypassed).
    171  f080							; ==============================================================================
    172  f080				   TitleBand
    173  f080							; ==================================================================
    174  f080							; Band 1 (36 lines): stage middle row — PREVIEW ONLY, no text.
    175  f080							; Same store order as the cave .Row (PF0, PF1, COLUPF, ENABL, PF2 last)
    176  f080							; so the band-transition line keeps the left half on band 0.
    177  f080							; ==================================================================
    178  f080							; Cave band 0 leaves the missiles latched (the .AfterRows clear is
    179  f080							; skipped on the title) and may leave the player's last GRP row live:
    180  f080							; clear GRP with VDEL OFF first (a GRP write while VDELP=1 only reaches
    181  f080							; the delayed slot — AGENTS "VDEL stale live-slot"). The missiles STAY
    182  f080							; on: band 1 is a real room preview, so a latched M1 strip is the room's
    183  f080							; own geometry (band 2 clears it before the 48px text).
