   1693  fa26							; GetConnIdx RETIRED (C3, 2026-10-20): the four exit handlers moved to
   1694  fa26							; bank2 and read the connection record in-bank (LevelConnB2), so this pad's
   1695  fa26							; body had no caller. Deleting it (plus the bank0 `sta` half and this bank's
   1696  fa26							; `jmp` half) reclaimed 15 B here and removed a live-but-uncalled pad.
   1697  fa26
   1698  fa26							; ClearPFColumn — A = left-half col 0..19; LineCount ($84) = first row;
   1699  fa26							;   CollisionEndY = last row (inclusive). AND-clear that col's
   1700  fa26							;   PF bit in those rows only. Clobbers A/X/Y + CPCScratch ($89) — NO
   1701  fa26							;   CollisionX (plan 5.1: BombMarkWalls keeps its broken-wall count there
   1702  fa26							;   across the call). Same-bank rts tail: BombMarkWalls jsrs this directly;
   1703  fa26							;   the old CallPad_ClearPFColumn path died with ApplyBombWalls (dead pad
   1704  fa26							;   kept).
   1705  fa26							;   Scratched retargeted Temp ($AD = bank0 TickCounter!) → $89 (plan 5.1b,
   1706  fa26							;   2026-10-20): every punch used to write the 60-frame game timer, and the
   1707  fa26							;   cell punch calls this up to 24×/blast instead of 2×, so the aliasing had
   1708  fa26							;   to go. $89 was RcBase; the rect cache has no reader since 5.1b.
   1709  fa26				   ClearPFColumn
   1710  fa26		       a8		      tay		; Y = col
   1711  fa27		       b9 57 fa 	      lda	BombClearMask,Y
   1712  fa2a		       85 89		      sta	CPCScratch	; AND mask (clear bit; NOT CollisionX)
   1713  fa2c		       a6 84		      ldx	LineCount	; first row
   1714  fa2e				   .CPCLoop
   1715  fa2e		       98		      tya		; col
