   2033  fbda							; ========================================================================
   2034  fbda							; Cross-bank call pads — 2026-10-20 (chunk 4): SPLIT across the banks, no
   2035  fbda							; twin. kernel.asm holds the eleven `sta $1FFx` halves compactly at
   2036  fbda							; $FBFC..$FC1C; after the switch the fetch at A+3 lands HERE, so this bank
   2037  fbda							; keeps only the `jmp` halves (at A+3, i.e. $FBFF onward). The reverse halves
   2038  fbda							; were dead bytes: no bank1/bank2/bank3 code calls a CallPad (guard:
   2039  fbda							; verify_build.check_callpads rejects any `jsr/jmp CallPad_*` outside
   2040  fbda							; kernel.asm). F6 hotspot ignores the written value, so a pad still passes
   2041  fbda							; A/X/Y/flags through untouched (`sta` affects no flag).
   2042  fbda							;   $FBFF <-$FBFC+3 UpdateBombSound	  $FC0E <-$FC0B+3 AddScore
   2043  fbda							;   $FC02 <-$FBFF+3 UpdateJetSound	  $FC11 <-$FC0E+3 IsRoomDark
   2044  fbda							;   $FC05 <-$FC02+3 BombSndDrop	  $FC14 <-$FC11+3 SetRoomDark
   2045  fbda							;   $FC08 <-$FC05+3 BombSndExplode	  $FC17 <-$FC14+3 UpdateLaserSound
   2046  fbda							;   ($FC0B retired by C3)		 $FC1D <-$FC1A+3 BombMarkWalls
   2047  fbda							; $FC1A (BuildColupF's +3) belongs to BANK3 — its pad is `sta $1FF7`.
